{
 "name": "VCSL World (music-production build)",
 "comment": "Built from the Versilian Community Sample Library (VCSL) by Versilian Studios, CC0 1.0. Source: https://github.com/sgossner/VCSL at c1ea7bcc3c7309650ab0da9d15c9cd1fbc4a4c7e. Folk harp (0:46), strumstick (0:25), dan tranh (0:107, vibrato 1:107, tremolo 2:107), psaltery plucked (0:15) and bowed (1:15), kalimbas and mbira (0:108 Tanzania, 1:108 Kenya, 2:108 Nyamaropa), balafon (0:12, soft mallets 1:12), hand chimes (0:14), wine glasses (0:92) and a world percussion kit on bank 128 program 25 (frame drums, claps, cajon, darbuka, cowbells, bongos, congas, agogo, cabasa, shakers, guiro, claves, slit drum, brake drum, anvil, finger cymbals, bell tree, ratchet, ocean drum; keys in references/soundbanks.md). Changes: pitch-checked against file names, small intonation offsets as fineTune, leading silence trimmed, levels matched per layer, 16-bit TPDF dither. Build b2: on the folk harp, each half-octave band of a take from 1 kHz up is taken out once it has come down to the recording's hiss, never in the first 0.06 s of a note (close_hiss): a plucked string's upper partials die first, and what those bands held afterwards was hiss, heard under a soft passage played alone. Every other preset is bit for bit that of b1.",
